Managing Resource Groups: 
Create Resource Group with that resource group's name.
az group create -- name MyResourceGroup -- location eastus  

List all resource groups in tabular format.
az group list -- output table  

Show detailed infomation on target resource group.
az group show -- name MyResourceGroup  

Force deletion of a resource type in the target resource group
az group delete -- name MyResourceGroup -f Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines -- yes

Working with Resource Group Deployments:
Every deployment has to have a name.  

az deployment group create |
-- name MyDeployment |
-- resource-group MyResourceGroup |
-- template-file main.bicep |
-- parameters @parameters.json

List all deployments on target resource group.
az deployment group list -- resource-group MyResourceGroup  

Show detail information on specified deployment from target resource group.
az deployment group show -- name MyDeployment -- resource-group MyResourceGroup

Delete deployment record from target resource group, does not delete resources.
az deployment group delete -- name MyDeployment -- resource-group MyResourceGroup


Deployment Parameters: Inline
Allow passing values directly to the command line using key-value pairs
Use to specify a small number of parameters or when a parameters file is not needed  

az deployment group create |
-- resource-group MyResourceGroup \
-- template-file main.bicep |
-- parameters accountName='myuniquestorage' sku='Standard_LRS'


Deployment Parameters: Mixed Methods
Enables modular deployments, enabling reuse of configuration files
Overrides specific values directly or pulling dynamic data from external sources
Apply environment-specific configurations (via files) while making minor overrides  

az deployment group create |
-- resource-group MyResourceGroup |
-- template-file main.bicep |
-- parameters @storageParams.json |
-- parameters https://website/extraParams.json |
-- parameters minTlsVersion='TLS_1.2'





